export const priorityPhilosopherMisunderstandings:Record<string,string[]>={
  plato:['The Forms are not merely physical objects in another location; they answer a problem about intelligibility and standards.','A speech by Socrates or another dialogue character is not automatically Plato’s final doctrine.'],
  aristotle:['The “golden mean” is not a rule to choose the mathematical middle in every case.','Final causes do not mean every natural process consciously pursues a goal.'],
  augustine:['The Confessions is not only autobiography; its narrative is part of an argument about desire, memory, creation, and time.','Evil as privation does not mean suffering is unreal or morally unimportant.'],
  aquinas:['The Five Ways are not intended as five self-contained modern scientific proofs.','Aquinas does not treat faith as a substitute for reasoning; he carefully distinguishes their domains.'],
  descartes:['Methodic doubt is a temporary discipline for reconstruction, not Descartes’s final skepticism or a rule for paralysis in ordinary life.','The cogito is not simply the premise “I think” inserted into a syllogism, and it does not immediately establish a complete immortal self.','Descartes gives observation and experiment indispensable roles in identifying particular mechanisms even though metaphysics supplies general principles.','The senses guide embodied preservation and natural inquiry; their limits as foundations do not make them useless.','Real distinction is only half of the mind-body story: Descartes also treats the experienced union as primitive, though Elisabeth shows how little that solves interaction.','The animal-machine thesis is textually and ethically serious, but its implications for animal consciousness remain disputed.','Passions are naturally useful bodily orientations that can be trained, not irrational enemies to be eliminated.'],
  hume:['Humean skepticism does not require abandoning ordinary life, history, or scientific inquiry.','His claim that reason does not motivate by itself is not a claim that reasoning never matters in action.','The bundle account challenges a separately perceived simple self, but Hume’s Appendix does not present the unity problem as solved.','His analysis of causation does not deny events, mechanisms, or the practical legitimacy of causal investigation.','Sentimentalism does not make morality an arbitrary report of whatever an individual happens to feel.','Hume’s racial hierarchy is a retained part of his public human science, not a harmless line detached from his method.'],
  kant:['The categorical imperative is not merely “follow rules regardless of consequences.”','Transcendental idealism does not straightforwardly claim that the external world is an illusion.'],
  nietzsche:['“Will to power” is not a simple command to dominate other people or one uncontested metaphysical substance.','Perspectivism does not mean every opinion is equally good or that truth is irrelevant.','The “death of God” names a cultural crisis, not only an individual profession of atheism.','Master morality is not simply Nietzsche’s recommended moral code, and ressentiment is not a label for every protest against power.','The Übermensch is not a racial or biological master species, though its relation to hierarchy and cultivation remains disputed.','The Will to Power is a posthumous arrangement of notebooks, not a completed book Nietzsche authorized.'],
  wittgenstein:['“Meaning is use” is a methodological reminder, not a complete one-line theory of every kind of meaning.','The later philosophy does not simply ban difficult questions; it asks how language gives them their apparent force.'],
  heidegger:['Authenticity is not lifestyle individualism or freedom from all social relations.','The critique of technology is not a demand to reject devices and return to a premodern life.'],
  beauvoir:['“One is not born, but rather becomes, a woman” does not deny embodiment; it analyzes how embodiment acquires social meaning.','Beauvoir is not merely a commentator applying Sartre’s philosophy.'],
  foucault:['Foucault does not claim that power is possessed only by a ruling group or that resistance is impossible.','Calling a category historically produced does not mean its effects are unreal.']
};
